  <static seed="209" source="Library/Valdosta/APEX_Calculus/2.4/APEX_2.4_16.pg">
    <statement><p>Compute the derivative of the given function.</p>
<p><me>f(t) = \frac{1}{t^{2}} \left( \csc t + 5 \right)</me></p>
<p><m>f'(t) =</m><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>t^{-2}\mathopen{}\left(-\csc\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(t\right)+\left(-2\right)t^{-3}\mathopen{}\left(\csc\mathopen{}\left(t\right)+5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



Use the Product Rule.



<me>f'(t) = (t^{-2})(-\csc t \cot t) + (-2 t^{-3})(\csc t + 5).</me>


</solution>
